        <h3 class="model-title">The Greenfield</h3>
        <p>A five-room Cape Cod with dormers on the front, a small pediment over the door, and a one-car garage attached to one end. The house and garage together measured about 36 feet across. The living room, 11½ by 20½ feet, ran the full depth of the house, with the fireplace on the end wall; there was a dining room, a dining alcove, and two bedrooms upstairs. <em>American Builder</em> later reprinted the Greenfield as plan no. 113 in its national plan book for builders.</p>
