        <h3 class="model-title">The Williamsburg</h3>
        <p>The largest of the four: a full two-story center-hall Colonial, 40 feet wide including its attached garage. The front door sat under an arched portico with built-in benches, and there was a porch at the back. It had six rooms, a bath, and a downstairs lavatory. <em>Architectural Forum</em> listed one at $8,600.</p>
